invariant: INV-58
file: p256_sign.c
catches: p256_sign_test
reason: sign_hedged no longer refuses all-zero noise, which is what a
  random source that returns without writing leaves after rand_draw
  (INV-4). Every signature over one message is then the same bytes again,
  and nothing downstream notices. bin/p256_sign_test signs with zero
  noise and requires CH_ASSERT to fire.

--- old
        CH_ASSERT(!ct_memeq_public(noise, unwritten, P256_NOISE_LEN));
--- new
        (void)unwritten;
